                    =20
                        <p></p><p>Jeff Levi is a Partner in Deloitte Consul=
ting=E2=80=99s Casey Quirk practice, where he leads the firm=E2=80=99s inve=
stment management consulting services business and serves on the investment=
 management and real estate practice leadership team. He advises asset and =
wealth managers on a broad range of complex strategic issues, including gro=
wth strategy, business and operating model transformation, and technology s=
trategy.=E2=80=8B</p>
<p>=E2=80=8BLevi=E2=80=99s client portfolio spans some of the world=E2=80=
=99s largest and fastest-growing asset and wealth managers, leading alterna=
tives firms, and a diverse set of specialist boutiques across traditional a=
sset management, alternatives, wealth management, and fintech. He brings gl=
obal experience, having worked across South America, Asia, Europe, and Nort=
h America.=E2=80=8B</p>
<p>=E2=80=8BLevi led the development of Casey Quirk=E2=80=99s knowledge cen=
ter, a global research and intelligence platform for asset and wealth manag=
ers, and remains an active contributor to Deloitte and Casey Quirk thought =
leadership. His co-authored work includes&nbsp;<i>Transforming the Enterpri=
se: Attributes of Winning Firms in Wealth Management</i>,&nbsp;<i>An Indust=
ry Rearranged</i>,&nbsp;<i>Digital Wealth Manager of Today</i>,&nbsp;<i>Tec=
hnology for the C-Suite</i>,&nbsp;<i>Distribution 2.0</i>,&nbsp;<i>Survival=
 of the Fittest</i>, and&nbsp;<i>Retooling Intermediary Sales</i>. He is al=
so a frequent speaker at industry conferences and a sought-after commentato=
r for media and publications.=E2=80=8B</p>
<p>=E2=80=8BOutside&nbsp;of work, Levi has set a Guinness World Record, won=
 a CNBC game show, and traveled around the world by ship. Prior to joining =
Deloitte, he was a partner at Casey Quirk and a senior analyst at NERA Econ=
omic Consulting. He holds a bachelor=E2=80=99s degree in economics, summa c=
um laude, from Ithaca College, and an MBA from the Yale School of Managemen=
t.</p>
